From 13350cacc15ad32b667536fef3b101f26b3b35f7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Angel Martinez <110217098+anmartinez1256@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 03:16:10 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 43/43] Dispersive extensions: guard the packed hooks and
 report a refused packing

The packed hooks use GCC/clang vector extensions: they are now under
the same compiler guard as the rest of the vector code, with empty
stubs otherwise, so other compilers build the unpacked paths.

The memory limit (twice the field arrays) is counted per engine over
all dispersive extensions instead of per extension, and a packing that
is refused by the limit or by a failed allocation prints one line at
verbose 1 with the bytes needed, the limit and the bytes already
packed. OPENEMS_ADE_PACKED=0 is reported at verbose 2.

No arithmetic changes: results are identical to the commit before.

Generated-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic)
Signed-off-by: Angel Martinez <110217098+anmartinez1256@users.noreply.github.com>
